  "id": "Compound::DB01148 - Gene::27115",
  "verbalization": "Flavoxate is implicated in the regulation of 3',5'-cyclic-amp phosphodiesterase activity through its interaction with Pde8a, Pde8b, and Pde4c, all of which are known to participate in this enzymatic process. The evidence suggests that Flavoxate may exert its effects by binding to a common target, Pde8b or Pde8a, which in turn modulates the activity of Pde7b. This implies a potential mechanism where Flavoxate influences Pde7b through a shared pathway involving the regulation of cyclic AMP phosphodiesterase activity. The consistent involvement of Pde7b in this process, across multiple pathways, highlights its role as a downstream effector in the regulation of cyclic AMP levels. The integration of these findings supports the notion that Flavoxate may act through a common mechanism to influence Pde7b, potentially by modulating the activity of the phosphodiesterase complex.",
